From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: alpha test in the shaders also on legacy GL contexts

On a legacy (compatibility) context WineD3D left the alpha test to
fixed-function GL: its shaders skipped the test and only glAlphaFunc()
was set. But nothing ever enables GL_ALPHA_TEST (the blitter only
disables it), so D3DRS_ALPHATESTENABLE had no effect at all: in
Daemonica the leaves of trees and bushes were drawn as opaque quads
(Panfrost, desktop GL compatibility profile). A test drawing textures of
every alpha format with alpha test on let every texel through; with
blending they were right.

Test in the shaders, as on core contexts, whatever the context.
---
 dlls/wined3d/adapter_gl.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/adapter_gl.c b/dlls/wined3d/adapter_gl.c
index e33e27b..b8eb49b 100644
--- a/dlls/wined3d/adapter_gl.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/adapter_gl.c
@@ -4939,7 +4939,9 @@ static void wined3d_adapter_gl_init_d3d_info(struct wined3d_adapter_gl *adapter_
 
     d3d_info->wined3d_creation_flags = wined3d_creation_flags;
     d3d_info->emulated_flatshading = vertex_caps.emulated_flatshading;
-    d3d_info->ffp_alpha_test = !!gl_info->supported[WINED3D_GL_LEGACY_CONTEXT];
+    /* Nothing enables GL_ALPHA_TEST (the blitter only disables it), so the
+     * fixed-function test was never on: test in the shaders everywhere. */
+    d3d_info->ffp_alpha_test = false;
     d3d_info->shader_double_precision = !!(shader_caps.wined3d_caps & WINED3D_SHADER_CAP_DOUBLE_PRECISION);
     d3d_info->shader_output_interpolation = !!(shader_caps.wined3d_caps & WINED3D_SHADER_CAP_OUTPUT_INTERPOLATION);
     d3d_info->viewport_array_index_any_shader = !!gl_info->supported[ARB_SHADER_VIEWPORT_LAYER_ARRAY];
